{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790428549872,"sessionID":"ses_f222d70b1ffeq6ZWMjMwl1hx91","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_97ed871e49f54bf68b14c78f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 << 'PYEOF'\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nimg = Image.open('/workspace/assets/sprites/platformer.jpg')\nw, h = img.size\npixels = img.load()\n\n# Star coins in platformers have a very specific bright golden color\n# They are typically yellow-orange with bright highlights\n# Let me sample some areas to understand colors better\n# From my visual inspection of the image, let me check specific regions\n\n# The image shows a platformer level. Let me try a more targeted color range\n# for golden yellow coins\nfound = []\nfor y in range(h):\n    for x in range(w):\n        r, g, b = pixels[x, y]\n        # Golden coin: dominant R+G, low B, some orange component\n        # Typical star coin: very bright gold/orange\n        if r > 200 and g > 150 and b < 100 and (r - b) > 100:\n            found.append((x, y))\n\nprint(f\"Very bright yellow pixels: {len(found)}\")\n\n# Look at the image in sections to find coin clusters\n# Save a debug image showing found pixels\ndebug = Image.new('RGB', (w, h), (0, 0, 0))\ndebug_pixels = debug.load()\nfor x, y in found:\n    debug_pixels[x, y] = (255, 0, 0)\ndebug.save('/workspace/yellow_debug.png')\n\n# Let me also look for the coin shape - star coins have a distinctive pattern\n# They're usually composed of a bright golden circle with a star pattern\n# Let me look for regions with high concentration of yellow pixels in a small radius\nprint(\"\\nLooking for dense yellow clusters (coin-like):\")\n\n# Use a sliding window approach\nfor y_step in range(0, h, 10):\n    for x_step in range(0, w, 10):\n        count = 0\n        for dy in range(-15, 16):\n            for dx in range(-15, 16):\n                ny, nx = y_step + dy, x_step + dx\n                if 0 <= nx < w and 0 <= ny < h:\n                    r, g, b = pixels[nx, ny]\n                    if r > 200 and g > 150 and b < 100 and (r - b) > 100:\n                        count += 1\n        if count > 100:\n            print(f\"  Dense cluster at ({x_step}, {y_step}): {count} yellow pixels in 31x31 window\")\nPYEOF"},"output":"Very bright yellow pixels: 5637\n\nLooking for dense yellow clusters (coin-like):\n  Dense cluster at (410, 60): 109 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (420, 60): 213 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (430, 60): 218 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (440, 60): 127 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (310, 70): 171 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (320, 70): 203 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (330, 70): 155 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (410, 70): 160 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (420, 70): 312 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (430, 70): 317 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (440, 70): 180 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (310, 80): 272 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (320, 80): 314 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (330, 80): 238 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (370, 80): 138 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (380, 80): 194 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (390, 80): 180 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (410, 80): 151 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (420, 80): 293 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (430, 80): 298 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (440, 80): 166 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (300, 90): 105 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (310, 90): 259 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (320, 90): 301 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (330, 90): 225 yellow pixels in 31x31 window\n  Dense cluster at (370,